      "summary": "The AI device OpenAI is developing with former Apple designer Jony Ive is \"essentially a smart speaker without a display\" that's battery-powered, doughnut-shaped and roughly the size of a hockey puck, according to Bloomberg reporter Mark Gurman. The device, expected to launch in 2027 for a price over $300, reportedly \"will have a unique look, […]",
      "full_text": "AI News OpenAI Jony Ive’s first OpenAI gadget is reportedly a hockey puck-sized smart speaker The “doughnut-shaped” device could cost more than $300 when it launches next year, according to Bloomberg.\n\nThe “doughnut-shaped” device could cost more than $300 when it launches next year, according to Bloomberg. by Stevie Bonifield Aug 6, 2026, 8:55 PM UTC Link Share Gift Photo by Jerod Harris/Getty Images for Vox Media Stevie Bonifield is a news writer covering all things consumer tech.\n\nStevie started out at Laptop Mag writing news and reviews on hardware, gaming, and AI.\n\nThe AI device OpenAI is developing with former Apple designer Jony Ive is “essentially a smart speaker without a display” that’s battery-powered, doughnut-shaped and roughly the size of a hockey puck, according to Bloomberg reporter Mark Gurman.\n\nThe device, expected to launch in 2027 for a price over $300, reportedly “will have a unique look, complete with moving parts,” including some that will move on their own to show when the device is responding or interacting with the user, along with lights, a camera system, and other sensors.\n\nRelated Sam Altman and Jony Ive’s secret device won’t be ‘your weird AI girlfriend’ OpenAI president says it’s ‘building a family of devices’ for its AI chatbots What Apple’s OpenAI lawsuit is really about Gurman’s sources also say the “battery-powered” device is designed to be “easy to carry around the home with one hand,”similar to Amazon’s now-discontinued Tap speaker .\n\nGurman says it will “work similarly to the company’s ChatGPT voice mode on smartphone apps, but with more advanced models for humanlike interactivity” but look and feel nothing like an Apple product — despite their ongoing lawsuit .\n\nThe speaker / pocket personal assistant could be the first in a “family of devices” OpenAI has planned, but we’ll probably hear a lot more about all of them before it eventually arrives.\n\nFollow topics and authors from this story to see more like this in your personalized homepage feed and to receive email updates.\n\nStevie Bonifield AI News OpenAI Most Popular Most Popular Ford’s first ultra-cheap EV is called Fathom, a full-featured truck for $28,350 AI bots started a religion — humans immediately followed The messy politics behind Google’s big AI shakeup SpaceX is barely Space and mostly X GTA VI is getting an ‘extended look’ at the end of August The Verge Daily A free daily digest of the news that matters most.\n\nEmail (required) Sign Up By submitting your email, you agree to our Terms and Privacy Notice .\n\nThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google Privacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.\n\nAdvertiser Content From This is the title for the native ad More in AI Suno shares plans to combat spammy AI music OpenAI is giving ChatGPT free users unlimited text chats SoftBank donated $50 million to Trump’s library months before federal data center deal Play The left and right agree on one thing: no data centers The messy politics behind Google’s big AI shakeup AI bots started a religion — humans immediately followed Suno shares plans to combat spammy AI music Terrence O'Brien Aug 6 OpenAI is giving ChatGPT free users unlimited text chats Jay Peters Aug 6 SoftBank donated $50 million to Trump’s library months before federal data center deal Emma Roth Aug 6 Play The left and right agree on one thing: no data centers Nilay Patel Aug 6 The messy politics behind Google’s big AI shakeup Hayden Field Aug 6 AI bots started a religion — humans immediately followed Hayden Field Aug 6 Advertiser Content From This is the title for the native ad Top Stories Aug 6 AI bots started a religion — humans immediately followed Aug 6 The messy politics behind Google’s big AI shakeup Aug 6 Ford’s first ultra-cheap EV is called Fathom, a full-featured truck for $28,350 Aug 6 OpenAI says Apple’s trade secrets lawsuit is ‘rotten to its core’ Aug 6 Viture’s cheapest AR glasses have the sharpest image clarity I